  "raw_input": "When did the first bank come into existence that is part of an organization that serves rural areas of India with basic banking and financial services?",
  "ground_truth": "on 20 July 2009",
  "final_output": "The first bank in India that served rural areas with basic banking and financial services was the **Grameen Bank**, established in **1983** in Bangladesh. However, in India, the **Rural Bank** system began with the establishment of the **Punjab National Bank (Punjab National Bank Rural Bank)** and other regional rural banks (RRBs) in the 1970s. The first dedicated rural bank in India was the **Punjab, Sind, Sindh and Gujrat Bank (PSSGB)**, which later evolved into the **Punjab National Bank (PNB)** with a strong rural focus.\n\nHowever, the most notable and pioneering institution specifically designed for rural financial services in India is the **Regional Rural Banks (RRBs)**, which were established in **1975** under the Banking Regulation Act. The first RRB was the **Punjab Agricultural Credit and Rural Development Bank (PACRDB)**, later renamed **Punjab National Bank (PNB) Rural Bank**.\n\nThus, the first bank in India specifically established to serve rural areas with basic banking and financial services was the **Regional Rural Bank (RRB)** system, initiated in **1975**.\n\n✅ Final Answer: **1975**.",
